          "title": "You'll want to know: नब्ज़",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "नब्ज़ — nabz — \"the pulse\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "नब्ज़ (nabz) is a loan from Arabic nabḍ, \"pulse, a throbbing\", which reached Hindi through Persian. Its Arabic root is n-b-ḍ (Lane)."
            }
          ]
        },
